**Definition (Standing cells)** · `def:compiler:standing-cells` fold_cells revalidates complete acts and partitions the cumulative completed boundary set, including earlier accepted acts under ``post:epoch:final-edge-set``, under network-v0.31.0, ``def:epoch:standing-fold-cell`` and ``def:epoch:net-stance``. Its key retains author, family and the sorted full role incidence, which includes source and terminal target. Opinion and Reference aggregate; settlement records, controls and home-only families remain singleton cells. Invitation currently returns the whole-result edition hold (`[ROOT-open:design:invitation-withdrawal-edition]`). The release now settles it through ``lem:epoch:authored-vouch-withdrawable``: the next implementation must fold Invitation by author-bundle netting, weigh exact cancellation home at zero and keep De-invite singleton at self with coefficient one; ``ver:membership:invitation-netting`` supplies the cases. Every member identity survives, and a paired act is one member, never independently folded legs. Mandatory coordinates are summed exactly before one clip to the signed unit interval. The operation changes no history, count, debit or title and reads no title premise. Rational spellings are internal carriers, not canonical publication bytes.

**Amendment (Cell evidence)** · `amend:compiler:cell-evidence` (`claim:compiler:cells-retain-members-and-sum-before-clipping`) compares literal rational tables, cancellation and reversed input, with each member still charged and counted. (`claim:compiler:cells-key-full-incidence-and-excluded-identities`) distinguishes complete Reference incidence, author and target and Affinity singletons. (`claim:compiler:invitation-cells-await-withdrawal-edition`) witnesses the whole-result hold without deleting an accepted act.

**Definition (Cell coefficients)** · `def:compiler:cell-coefficients` coefficient reads the mandatory-coordinate census of all nineteen families from network-v0.31.0, ``rem:epoch:compiled-acts-fold-into-cells``. The geometric mean uses magnitudes under ``def:epoch:effective-act-contribution``: the empty set is one, any exact zero gives zero, and hostility costs the same as support. Participant uses interactivity and responsibility, not continuity; Invitation lists urgency and formality, not its T-leg relevance, but remains an edition hold before evaluation. One coordinate is exact magnitude; two coordinates require the square root of their reduced rational product. Perfect-square numerator and denominator return an exact rational through the existing bounded arithmetic. Otherwise a typed irrational-evidence hold retains the radicand; no approximation escapes. A decimal integer-root check is prepaid by the same rational arithmetic budget, introduces no dependency or identity recipe, and is separate from independent test tables. Unknown families, incomplete coordinate maps and values outside the signed unit interval refuse. This prices a supplied folded cell and does not resolve recipients or establish a standing row.

**Amendment (Coefficient evidence)** · `amend:compiler:coefficient-evidence` (`claim:compiler:mandatory-coordinate-census-covers-nineteen-families`) compares a literal family table. (`claim:compiler:coefficients-are-exact-or-held-with-numeric-evidence`) compares exact means, hostile magnitudes, zero, a finite independent integer-square table, large perfect squares and independently squared rational bounds around an irrational probe. (`claim:compiler:coefficient-inputs-are-bounded-and-complete`) distinguishes malformed inputs from numeric-evidence holds.

**Definition (Recipient resolution)** · `def:compiler:recipient-resolution` resolve_recipients derives cumulative cells, Registration anchors and persistent title events from the same validated history at a positive boundary under network-v0.31.0, ``def:epoch:standing-recipient-resolution`` and ``tbl:epoch:standing-recipient-resolution``. Formation establishes complete author-owned incidence and declared approval; no terminal artifact ownership fold is read. Strictly positive mandatory coordinates permit an Opinion or complete Reference to Profile to resolve to that Profile's anchored Actor. Other artifact and control families resolve home, including Affinity and Join Request. Accept and Ratify resolve to the counterparty only through a title-transferring event, with live consent and certified seller authorization established by recognition. Conflicts, cancellation, wrong parties and attempts reusing consumed records create no new outward event; successful events survive consumption and resale under ``post:epoch:settlement-standing-title-coupling``. A non-positive coordinate or target without a Registration anchor in the completed set resolves home. Invitation currently holds the whole result under (`[ROOT-open:design:invitation-withdrawal-edition]`). The released ``lem:epoch:authored-vouch-withdrawable`` requires Invitation netting and home resolution at coefficient zero on cancellation; ``prop:epoch:net-stance-properties`` requires dependency-compliant permutation invariance. Those implementation obligations remain with the graph lane. Every cell and member identity remains in the result; this chooses destinations, not coefficients, source emission or allocation amounts. Public verifier and exact-arithmetic limits remain explicit inputs; no partner-clause placement premise remains. No canonical encoding or commitment recipe is introduced.

